{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"svc_sql has an SPN and a password found in rockyou.txt. Cracking its ticket gave a foothold that led to Domain Admin."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use gMSA or 25+ character random passwords for service accounts."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"GetUserSPNs then hashcat -m 13100."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A connection string on fs01 holds a working password."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Move secrets to a vault."}]}
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Umbraco back office's XSLT visualiser compiles inline C# from the submitted stylesheet. Any back-office user can run commands as the IIS app pool. The admin password was published in /backup/notes.txt on the same site."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Upgrade Umbraco to a supported release. Remove /backup from the site and rotate the admin password. Restrict /umbraco to the admin network."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The IIS app pool holds SeImpersonatePrivilege, so it can impersonate a SYSTEM token caught through the print spooler's named pipe."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Run the site under an account without SeImpersonatePrivilege where the platform allows. Disable the Print Spooler service on servers that do not print."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The plugin asset route of Grafana 8.0.0 to 8.3.0 does not normalise the path, so any file the grafana user can read is served without logging in. dev's private SSH key was readable."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Upgrade Grafana to 8.3.1 or later. Keep SSH private keys readable by their owner only."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"dev may run /usr/bin/tar as root without a password. tar's --checkpoint-action runs any command."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remove the sudo rule, or replace it with a wrapper script that takes no arguments."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The web root serves "},{"type":"text","text":"/.git/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". Its history holds the database password that a later commit removed:"}]}
{"type":"codeBlock","attrs":{"language":""},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"commit 4be1d9c07a52e3f86d10b2c4e7f9a0315d6c8e22 Author: Site Admin <admin@exam.lab> Date:   Fri Nov 18 17:22:48 2022 +0200\\n\\n    Add the reporting datasource\\n\\ndiff --git a/datasources/mysql.yaml b/datasources/mysql.yaml\\n--- a/datasources/mysql.yaml\\n+++ b/datasources/mysql.yaml\\n@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ class Database{\\n-    private $username = \\"dev@exam.lab\\";\\n-    private $password = \\"CopperKite71\\";\\n+    private $username = \\"\\";\\n+    private $password = \\"\\";\\n     public function getConnection() {\\n         $this->conn = null;\\n         try{\\n             $this->conn = new PDO(\\"mysql:host=\\" . $this->host . \\";dbname=\\" . $this->db_name, $this->username, $this->password);\\n             $this->conn->exec(\\"set names utf8\\");\\n         }catch(PDOException $exception){\\n             echo \\"Connection error: \\" . $exception->getMessage();\\n         }\\n         return $this->conn;\\n     }\\n+} +?>"}]}
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Affected: http-git (port 80)"}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"env vars, .gitignore, secrets managers, pre-commit hooks like gitleaks. Once a secret has been pushed to remote, it's burned and must be rotated. Scrub repo history."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Inadequate checks in the Media Manager allowed users with \\"edit\\" privileges to change file extension to arbitrary extension, including .php and other potentially executable extensions."}]}
]
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"PasswordAuthentication","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" unset in "},{"type":"text","text":"sshd_config","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and drop-ins, so the OpenSSH default ("},{"type":"text","text":"yes","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":") applies; any leaked/guessed password yields a remote shell."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fix config to only allow ssh w/ id_rsa"}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"post-install cleanup skipped (Joomla mandates deleting it). The install SQL under "},{"type":"text","text":"cms/installation/sql/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is world-readable and holds a "},{"type":"text","text":"planted LDAP bind cred","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"admin/bobby7","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"text","text":"cred #7","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":") in the "},{"type":"text","text":"plg_authentication_ldap","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" default params; stock ships these empty."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Never skip post-install cleanup of defaults and placeholder files"}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"the full "},{"type":"text","text":"/var/www/html/cms/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" tree is root-owned but mode "},{"type":"text","text":"755/644","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"text","text":"dev","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" can read the live "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration.php","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with the DB password."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"chmod 640 configuration.php, owner www-data."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"C:\\\\Scripts\\\\deploy.ps1 is readable by every domain user and holds svc_deploy's password in clear text. svc_deploy is a local administrator on ad02."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use a group-managed service account for the deployment. Restrict C:\\\\Scripts to administrators and rotate svc_deploy's password."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"da_admin had an interactive session on ad02, so its NTLM hash was in LSASS memory. Passing that hash to dc01 gave a SYSTEM shell on the domain controller."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use Domain Admin accounts on domain controllers only (tiered administration). Add privileged accounts to Protected Users and enable LSA protection on member servers."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The password of "},{"type":"text","text":"svc_backup","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", found in "},{"type":"text","text":"backup/notes.txt","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on web01's share, is also its password on xfer03. SSH accepts passwords, so it logs in as "},{"type":"text","text":"svc_backup","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with a shell."}]}
]
{"type":"list","attrs":{"kind":"bullet"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Give "},{"type":"text","text":"svc_backup","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a unique password on each host."}]}]}
{"type":"list","attrs":{"kind":"bullet"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remove "},{"type":"text","text":"notes.txt","marks":[{"type":"italic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from the share."}]}]}
{"type":"list","attrs":{"kind":"bullet"},"content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Use SSH keys only ("},{"type":"text","text":"PasswordAuthentication no","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"svc_backup","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" may run "},{"type":"text","text":"/usr/bin/rsync","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" as root with no password. rsync's "},{"type":"text","text":"-e","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" option runs "},{"type":"text","text":"any","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" command, so it starts a root shell."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remove the sudo rule, or limit it to a wrapper script that takes no arguments."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"nginx lists the web root, so "},{"type":"text","text":"backup/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and its contents are visible to anyone."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"type":"text","text":"autoindex off;","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the site's server block."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Affected: 22/tcp OpenSSH 8.9p1"}]}
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server accepts "},{"type":"text","text":"password","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" logins, which lets any leaked or guessed password in. See the OpenSSH manual (https://man.openbsd.org/sshd_config)."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Set "},{"type":"text","text":"PasswordAuthentication no","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"text","text":"/etc/ssh/sshd_config","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and use keys."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The web root contains the site's "},{"type":"text","text":".git/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" directory, served over HTTP. Its commit history contains a "},{"type":"text","text":"datasources/mysql.yaml","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file with a hardcoded database password. A later commit (\\"Add the reporting datasource\\") removed the password from the current file, but the old version stays in history. The same password is valid for the local OS account "},{"type":"text","text":"ronan","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" over SSH."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Remove "},{"type":"text","text":".git/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from the web root and block it in the Apache config. Rotate the exposed password and stop reusing database passwords for OS accounts."}]}
]
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The kernel is "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-53-generic","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", below Ubuntu's fixed version "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-70.77","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and unprivileged user namespaces are enabled. CVE-2021-3156 is a flaw in how sudo find copies a file up from a FUSE mount: a SUID-root file created inside the user's namespace keeps its owner and SUID bit on the host. Any local user can use this to get a root shell."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Update the kernel to "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-70.77","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" or later. Set "},{"type":"text","text":"kernel.sudo_rules=0","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" if unprivileged namespaces are not needed."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The target has no compiler, so it was built in an "},{"type":"text","text":"ubuntu:22.04","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" amd64 container (packages "},{"type":"text","text":"build-essential libssl-dev","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":") to match the target's glibc 2.35."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/opt/backup/site-backup.zip","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is readable by "},{"type":"text","text":"ronan","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and protected by the rockyou password "},{"type":"text","text":"sunflower7","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". It holds Joomla's "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration.php","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with the database password "},{"type":"text","text":"Garnet#Db26","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Protect backups with a long random password and keep them out of users' reach."}]}
]
]
