{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The server accepts "},{"type":"text","text":"password","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" logins, which lets any leaked or guessed password in. See the OpenSSH manual (https://man.openbsd.org/sshd_config)."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Set "},{"type":"text","text":"PasswordAuthentication no","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in "},{"type":"text","text":"/etc/ssh/sshd_config","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and use keys."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The web root contains the site's "},{"type":"text","text":".git/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" directory, served over HTTP. Its commit history contains a "},{"type":"text","text":"datasources/mysql.yaml","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" file with a hardcoded database password. A later commit (\\"Add the reporting datasource\\") removed the password from the current file, but the old version stays in history. The same password is valid for the local OS account "},{"type":"text","text":"ronan","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" over SSH."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Remove "},{"type":"text","text":".git/","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" from the web root and block it in the Apache config. Rotate the exposed password and stop reusing database passwords for OS accounts."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The kernel is "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-53-generic","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", below Ubuntu's fixed version "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-70.77","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and unprivileged user namespaces are enabled. CVE-2021-3156 is a flaw in how sudo find copies a file up from a FUSE mount: a SUID-root file created inside the user's namespace keeps its owner and SUID bit on the host. Any local user can use this to get a root shell."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Update the kernel to "},{"type":"text","text":"5.15.0-70.77","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" or later. Set "},{"type":"text","text":"kernel.sudo_rules=0","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" if unprivileged namespaces are not needed."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" The target has no compiler, so it was built in an "},{"type":"text","text":"ubuntu:22.04","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" amd64 container (packages "},{"type":"text","text":"build-essential libssl-dev","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":") to match the target's glibc 2.35."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"/opt/backup/site-backup.zip","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is readable by "},{"type":"text","text":"ronan","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and protected by the rockyou password "},{"type":"text","text":"sunflower7","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":". It holds Joomla's "},{"type":"text","text":"configuration.php","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":" with the database password "},{"type":"text","text":"Garnet#Db26","marks":[{"type":"code"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}
]
{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Label:","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Protect backups with a long random password and keep them out of users' reach."}]}
